{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Deliver me, I pray.</b> The word נא signifies a request and also signifies 'now' — meaning, lest Esau burst forth against him. And one might say that HaShem will indeed restore to him double all that he has; therefore he prayed before HaShem that He deliver him and establish in his hand what he had reached now, and that the hands of Esau not gain success, even though HaShem will afterward restore his captives." "<b>From the hand of my brother, etc.</b> Rashi, his memory for a blessing, explained 'my brother' as meaning: he does not deal with me as a brother but as Esau the wicked. Yet according to his words, his memory for a blessing, there was no need to say anything other than 'from the hand of my brother Esau,' and the matter is understood from his saying 'Esau' in addition, since he has no brother other than him." "However, he intended to pray, for Esau had two dimensions of strength: the first on account of the merit of Isaac, and the second on account of his great power and might, and great strength is needed to be saved from him. Therefore he prayed that the merit of the fathers not stand for him. And this is what he said, <b>Deliver me, I pray, from the hand of my brother</b> — even though Esau is a brother to Jacob, nevertheless I pray; and corresponding to the dimension of his great power he said <b>from the hand of Esau</b>, and he is known as exalted and uplifted." "<b>Further,</b> he may intend to say in this manner: <b>Deliver me, I pray, from the hand of my brother</b> — if he schemes against him to do harm with brotherly deceit, which is a path from which Jacob cannot save himself; <b>from the hand of Esau</b> — if he proclaims his wickedness to do harm — for this too prayer was needed to deliver him from his hand." "<b>Further,</b> he may intend to recall the wickedness of Esau: the first — <b>from the hand of my brother</b> — yet he seeks to kill his brother; is there a wicked one like this? And it is fitting to humble him before Jacob. And further — <b>from the hand of Esau</b> — who is publicly known for wickedness apart from this sin, and a righteous one should not falter before a wicked one."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:39.635517354Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}